1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-2--2a-learn-the-core-words","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-2/2a-learn-the-core-words","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-2/2a-learn-the-core-words","sourceHash":"fd287ef41c44031447e84ed7c47f77f9bc77e17541577b76e0fb95ad22c09433","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:43.136Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"2A — Learn the Core Words","zh":"2A——学习核心词汇"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You've finished the foundations and know roughly 1000 words. You have a daily routine, you're comfortable with the basic tools, and you can pick out the meaning of simple sentences. Now it's time to <strong>double</strong> your vocabulary.","zh":"你已经完成基础阶段，掌握了大约1000个词。你有固定的日常安排，熟悉基本工具，也能理解简单句子的大意。现在是时候<strong>将词汇量扩大一倍</strong>了。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The 2000 most common words in any language make up roughly 80% of everyday text. That means once you know them, the majority of what you read will be familiar — even if the remaining 20% still trips you up. Getting to 2000 words is the single biggest unlock for comprehension.","zh":"任何语言中最常见的2000个词，大约构成日常文本的80%。这意味着一旦掌握它们，你读到的大多数内容都会变得熟悉——即使剩下的20%仍会让你感到卡顿。达到2000词，是提升理解能力的最大单项突破。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your day-to-day activities don't change much from Phase 1. You're still doing vocab study, interactive immersion, and some freeflow immersion. The difference is that you're now working with harder content and pushing further into native materials.","zh":"你的日常活动与第一阶段相比不会有太大变化。你仍会学习词汇、进行互动沉浸，并进行一些自由流沉浸。不同之处在于，你现在接触的是更难的内容，并进一步深入母语内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If your target language shares a lot of vocabulary with a language you already know (like English speakers learning French or Spanish), this sub-phase may go quickly — many words will already be partially familiar as cognates, so you basically already know them.","zh":"如果你的目标语言与一门你已经掌握的语言共享大量词汇（例如英语使用者学习法语或西班牙语），这个子阶段可能会进展得很快——许多词作为同源词已经部分熟悉，所以你基本上早就认识它们了。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're learning a more distant language, it will take longer, but these languages tend to have well-made frequency resources to help. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">Categories of Language Difficulty</a>","zh":"如果你学习的是距离较远的语言，所需时间会更长，但这类语言通常有制作良好的词频资源可以提供帮助。 <a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">语言难度分类</a>"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are no new activities in this sub-phase. Instead, the focus is on leveling up how you use the tools you already have:","zh":"这一子阶段没有新的活动。相反，重点是提升你使用现有工具的方式："}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Vocabulary size matters.</strong> This is the phase where sheer word count has the biggest impact on your experience. Every hundred new words noticeably changes how much you understand. Keep working through a high-quality frequency list or deck. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki\">Learning Words with Anki</a> <a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">Vocabulary Size</a>","zh":"<strong>词汇量很重要。</strong> 这是单纯的词汇数量对学习体验影响最大的阶段。每增加一百个新词，你的理解程度都会明显提高。继续学习高质量的词频表或词汇牌组。 <a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-words-with-anki\">使用 Anki 学习词汇</a> <a href=\"/roadmap/library/vocabulary-size\">词汇量</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Transition to adult-level content.</strong> If you've been using beginner or learner content, start exploring native content made for adults — with tools. TV shows with target-language subtitles are ideal because they give you three channels of input at once: visual context, audio, and text. This combination makes things much more comprehensible than any single channel alone. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/hybrid-immersion-content\">Hybrid Immersion Content</a>","zh":"<strong>过渡到成人级内容。</strong> 如果你一直在使用初学者或学习者内容，可以开始探索面向成人制作的原生内容——并配合工具使用。带有目标语言字幕的电视剧非常理想，因为它们能同时提供三种输入渠道：视觉语境、音频和文字。这种组合比单独使用任何一种渠道都更容易理解。 <a href=\"/roadmap/library/hybrid-immersion-content\">混合型沉浸内容</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Use the comprehensibility factors to your advantage.</strong> Not all content is equally hard. A slice-of-life TV drama with clear dialogue and predictable plots is much easier than a fast-paced news show. Choose content where the visuals help tell the story and the language is relatively everyday. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/comprehensibility-factors\">Comprehensibility Factors</a>","zh":"<strong>善用影响可理解性的因素。</strong> 并非所有内容的难度都相同。一部对白清晰、情节可预测的日常生活类电视剧，要比节奏快速的新闻节目容易得多。选择视觉画面有助于讲述故事、语言也相对日常的内容。 <a href=\"/roadmap/library/comprehensibility-factors\">可理解性因素</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your time breakdown is similar to 1D, with a slight shift: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"你的时间分配与 1D 类似，但有一些调整： <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong> 25%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong> 50%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 25%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong> 25%"}]},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Interactive immersion is still the most important block. This is where you're actively working to understand and where the majority of your learning happens.","zh":"互动沉浸仍然是最重要的部分。在这里，你会主动努力去理解，而大部分学习也会发生在这个过程中。"}},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 20-25 mins","zh":"词汇学习：20–25 分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio (TV show with subtitles): 45 mins","zh":"带音频的互动阅读（带字幕的电视剧）：45 分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Reading with Audio (familiar or easier content): 20-25 mins","zh":"带音频的自由流阅读（熟悉或较简单的内容）：20–25 分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 2B when you:","zh":"满足以下条件时，进入 2B："}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Know approximately 2000 words","zh":"大约掌握 2000 个词"},{"en":"Can understand around 80% of the sentences in adult-level content when using subtitles and tools (dictionary, pausing, replaying)","zh":"使用字幕和工具（词典、暂停、回放）时，能够理解成人级内容中约 80% 的句子"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The claim that 2000 words cover roughly 80% of everyday text comes from foundational vocabulary research by <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/491314AA1B451AD04F3536000F1C9F0D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation (2001)</a>, updated in <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/25C481C771758930E8EBBE811231FEB7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation (2013)</a>. These coverage figures have been replicated across multiple languages and text types, though exact percentages vary depending on the language and corpus.","zh":"“2000 个词大致覆盖日常文本 80%”这一说法源自 <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/491314AA1B451AD04F3536000F1C9F0D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2001）</a>的基础词汇研究，并由 <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/learning-vocabulary-in-another-language/25C481C771758930E8EBBE811231FEB7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2013）</a>更新。这些覆盖率数据已在多种语言和文本类型中得到重复验证，不过具体百分比会因语言和语料库而有所不同。"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Why vocabulary size matters so much is well-established. <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-349-12396-4_12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Laufer (1992)</a>, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/09571730802389975\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stæhr (2008)</a>, and <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation (2006)</a> all demonstrated that vocabulary size is the single strongest predictor of reading comprehension in a second language — stronger than grammar knowledge, reading strategy, or prior knowledge. This is the empirical foundation for why reaching 2000 words is such a meaningful milestone.","zh":"词汇量为何如此重要，已有充分研究证明。<a href=\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-349-12396-4_12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Laufer（1992）</a>、<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/09571730802389975\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stæhr（2008）</a>和<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/cmlr.63.1.59\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nation（2006）</a>都证明，词汇量是第二语言阅读理解能力最强的单一预测因素——其影响强于语法知识、阅读策略或先备知识。这就是为什么达到 2000 个词是一个意义重大的里程碑的实证基础。"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The observation that cognate overlap and language families affect learning speed reflects research on language transfer by <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/language-transfer/0A19422B8005A10AFC282615FD542519\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Odlin (1989)</a>, who documented how similarities and differences between a learner's native language and target language predictably affect acquisition rates.","zh":"关于同源词重叠和语言家族会影响学习速度的观察，反映了 <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/language-transfer/0A19422B8005A10AFC282615FD542519\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Odlin（1989）</a>关于语言迁移的研究。他记录了学习者的母语与目标语言之间的相似之处和差异如何以可预测的方式影响习得速度。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
